# The public address of the site. Once its DNS records (A, and AAAA if the server has IPv6) point to the server:
# copy to ~/vigie/sites/public.caddy with the real name, set ORIGIN=https://<name> in ~/vigie/web.env, then
#   systemctl --user restart vigie-web caddy
# Caddy gets the certificate from Let's Encrypt by itself (ports 80 and 443 are open).
vigie.example.org {
	import site
	# Only when the answer has none: the site sends its own, the API does not.
	header ?Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
}

# With a "www." record too:
# www.vigie.example.org {
# 	redir https://vigie.example.org{uri} permanent
# }
